Used for solo [[utaite|utaite]]s who generally operate independently, similar to the [[indie virtual youtuber|indie virtual youtuber]] tag.

If the indie Utaite in question is:

- part of a broader Utaite group consisting of at least one more Utaite, the copyright tag instead would be that of that given group, to account for the (hash)tags that the individual character tags couldn't include under their wiki's Other Names;
- sharing a channel with at least one (1) more Utaite, the copyright tag would be of the channel instead, for similar reasons as above;
- sharing an agency/company with at least one (1) more Utaite that has a tag on site, the copyright tag would be of that given agency instead;
- depicted with their real self and not their online persona, and they don't meet any of the above criteria, they should be tagged with [[real life|real life]] instead of this tag;

Due to the flexible nature of utaite, being able to be independent or affiliated with agencies/corporate entities at a given moment, this tag can also serve as a "solo utaite" tag, as to not lead to the sudden creation of needless company tags. Previously, these utaite were tagged under the site they originated from (e.g. [[niconico|niconico]]).

A solo [[virtual youtuber|virtual youtuber]] who is not affiliated directly with a (major) corporate group, and is thus independent.

If the indie Virtual YouTuber(s) in question is:

- part of a broader VTuber group consisting of at least one more VTuber, the copyright tag instead would be that of that given group, to account for the (hash)tags that the individual character tags couldn't include under their wiki's Other Names;
- sharing a channel with at least one (1) more VTuber, the copyright tag would be of the channel instead, for similar reasons as above;
- under a corporate support group (i.e. VirtuaReal Link, etc.), depending on the circumstance, they receive their own copyright tag, due to the nature of their affiliation with said corporate entity and the potential for them to just leave it if they wanted to;

This tag can also alternatively serve as a pseudo-[[original|original]] tag, allowing one to use both the relevant request tags, if they are uncertain about the VTuber and their affiliations.

